+# Temporary automation testing — Mo, 2026-10-15
+
+**Do not mistake this for the production hiring design.** Mo explicitly requests
+that the Crew Office always have a fisherman and a deckhand so automation can
+be tested now, including on existing saves.
+
+`GameData.AlwaysOfferTestCrew = true` enables `GameState.EnsureTestCrewOffers()`.
+It fills missing roles when the board rolls, after hiring, and when loading old
+saves. Offers remain visible even when the boat is full; hiring still obeys normal
+fees, two rowboat crew slots, three skiff slots and contract durations. No free
+crew, player money injection, permanent contracts or player-save reset.
+
+For the current test slice the starter rowboat accepts two hired employees plus
+the captain. A fisherman unlocks the existing second rod socket and claims that
+rod, leaving the first rod for the captain. A deckhand carries and baits. The
+captain stays at the rod after a catch with a prominent Throw again / Leave
+choice; Throw starts the next cast without reselecting a world bubble.
+
+To restore the random production board, set `AlwaysOfferTestCrew` to false and
+update `UrgentCrewChecks` and shop testing copy. Existing offers remain until the
+next normal board roll. Decide separately whether to restore the rowboat's old
+one-crew/tier restriction; that capacity is currently changed at Mo's request.
+The intended production progression still introduces fisherman automation on the
+skiff. Preserve that intent in future balance work.
+
+The following recovery/reward improvements are **normal gameplay**, not crew-shop
+test overrides: unlimited poor scraps when paid bait runs out (only small herring
+and mackerel), explicit port selling with an exact payout preview, saved unsold
+haul, live haul value/freshness and a 60-second freshness grace from landing.
+Harbour storage freezes the remaining sale value. Sell before setting sail again;
+crew/contracts advance once at sale (or arrival for an empty trip).
+
+Verification: `FirstVoyageChecks.Regression` includes `UrgentCrewChecks.Run`:
+real fisherman/deckhand simulation without captain input, two-crew limit, test
+board across seeds and old saves, scraps bounds, persistent cast interaction,
+unsold-haul save/reload, quote/sale equality, no duplicate sale and freshness.
+Native preview captures support `-capture-voyage <directory> -capture-urgent`.
+The capture fixture funds its own save-isolated hire actions; normal play does not.
